   "answer": "Tract movements shape the passage containing vibrating air, changing the resulting sound. **Acoustic phonetics studies that sound and its relationship to production**.\n\nChanges in tract shape alter how that air can vibrate. The resulting acoustic pattern carries information about the speech movements that shaped the passage.",
