   "wordings": {
    "original": "How do voicing, place and manner contribute different information about a consonant?",
    "college": "How do voicing, place and manner contribute different information about a consonant?",
    "simple": "How do voicing, place and manner contribute different information about a consonant?"
   },
   "answer": "Voicing concerns vocal-fold vibration, place concerns the constriction location and manner concerns its type. **They supply distinct physical dimensions**.\n\nVoicing concerns vocal-fold vibration, place concerns the location of a constriction, and manner concerns its type. An oral stop blocks and releases the mouth airflow, while a fricative maintains a narrow noisy passage.",
