   "topic": "rate",
   "concept": "rate",
   "prompt": "Why does a larger learning rate change both speed and variability?",
   "wordings": {
    "original": "Why does a larger learning rate change both speed and variability?",
    "college": "Why does a larger learning rate change both speed and variability?",
    "simple": "Why does a larger learning rate change both speed and variability?"
   },
   "answer": "A larger rate makes each observation produce a bigger correction. **It increases adjustment speed and the influence of sample variation**.\n\nLarge corrections can approach a target quickly but can also follow random sample variation more strongly. Small corrections change the estimate more slowly and usually make the path steadier in this example.",
