   "type": "written",
   "topic": "closure",
   "concept": "closure",
   "prompt": "How does a cloze task transfer the completion problem to a sequence?",
   "wordings": {
    "original": "How does a cloze task transfer the completion problem to a sequence?",
    "college": "How does a cloze task transfer the completion problem to a sequence?",
    "simple": "How does a cloze task transfer the completion problem to a sequence?"
   },
   "answer": "A cloze task withholds part of a sequence and asks for a fitting completion. **The surrounding relationships constrain the missing part**.\n\nA cloze task removes part of a sequence and asks for a suitable completion. Completing it well requires using relationships among the available parts rather than responding to each part independently.",
