   "lectureId": "lecture03",
   "moduleId": "module1",
   "type": "written",
   "topic": "next token",
   "concept": "next-token",
   "prompt": "What stays the same when next-item prediction is applied to different kinds of vectors?",
   "wordings": {
    "original": "What stays the same when next-item prediction is applied to different kinds of vectors?",
    "college": "What stays the same when next-item prediction is applied to different kinds of vectors?",
    "simple": "What stays the same when next-item prediction is applied to different kinds of vectors?"
   },
   "answer": "The items are represented as ordered vectors and the task predicts a continuation from context. **Their original materials can differ without changing that general organization**.\n\nThe model uses the available context to assign probabilities to possible continuations. Learning improves those probabilities when the actual continuation supplies feedback.",
