   "answer": "Recognition uses current representations to identify an input, while learning changes those representations. **Using knowledge differs from acquiring it**.\n\nRecognition uses current representations to identify an input, while learning changes those representations after experience. An account of knowing must connect what the system has learned to the decisions it can make.",
