   "topic": "octopus",
   "concept": "octopus",
   "prompt": "What relationship makes complex motor behavior comparable with speaking?",
   "wordings": {
    "original": "What relationship makes complex motor behavior comparable with speaking?",
    "college": "What relationship makes complex motor behavior comparable with speaking?",
    "simple": "What relationship makes complex motor behavior comparable with speaking?"
   },
   "answer": "Both coordinate many moving parts around an action. **The organization of the parts is the shared relationship**, despite different organs and goals.\n\nSmaller action patterns can combine into a complex motor sequence. Their order and coordination help make the full action effective in the current environment.",
   "rubric": [],
