   "lectureId": "lecture03",
   "moduleId": "module1",
   "type": "written",
   "topic": "speech",
   "concept": "speech",
   "prompt": "What does articulatory phonetics study about the hidden movements of speaking?",
   "wordings": {
    "original": "What does articulatory phonetics study about the hidden movements of speaking?",
    "college": "What does articulatory phonetics study about the hidden movements of speaking?",
    "simple": "What does articulatory phonetics study about the hidden movements of speaking?"
   },
   "answer": "It studies **how the speech organs move and configure the tract**. Those physical actions supply the articulatory description of a sound.\n\nThe movements must work together, because changing one part alters the air passage available to the others. Direct visual feedback is limited, yet the developing speaker learns a large vocabulary and increasingly adult-like coordination.",
