   "moduleId": "module1",
   "type": "written",
   "topic": "learning",
   "concept": "learning",
   "prompt": "What must happen after a wrong prediction for learning to occur?",
   "wordings": {
    "original": "What must happen after a wrong prediction for learning to occur?",
    "college": "What must happen after a wrong prediction for learning to occur?",
    "simple": "What must happen after a wrong prediction for learning to occur?"
   },
   "answer": "The prediction must be compared with a training objective and used to change the parameters. **An unchanged repeated calculation alone does not teach the target relationship**.\n\nComparing a prediction with its target reveals a mismatch. Repeated corrections change how future inputs are processed, so later responses can become more appropriate.",
