   "topic": "initial estimate",
   "concept": "initial-estimate",
   "prompt": "Why can opposite directions of movement both reduce error?",
   "wordings": {
    "original": "Why can opposite directions of movement both reduce error?",
    "college": "Why can opposite directions of movement both reduce error?",
    "simple": "Why can opposite directions of movement both reduce error?"
   },
   "answer": "A guess above the target improves by moving down, while one below improves by moving up. **Improvement concerns a smaller discrepancy, not one fixed numerical direction**.\n\nA starting value above the target must generally move downward, while one below it must generally move upward. In both cases the objective is a smaller discrepancy, not a particular direction on the graph.",
