   "answer": "The tongue and lips alter the location and shape of the air passage. **That changes the tract resonances associated with vowel quality**.\n\nA high front tongue position produces the vowel in dean, while a high back position with rounded lips produces the vowel in dune. A lower tongue configuration produces a more open vowel such as the one represented by /a/.",
