   "answer": "The neuron multiplies each input activation by its connection weight and adds the contributions. **The result is a weighted sum**.\n\nA positive weight preserves the sign of an incoming activation, while a negative weight reverses it. Its magnitude controls the strength of the contribution, so a large weight is not automatically a good weight.",
